{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair reconcile.py to join payments to invoices, aggregate multiple payments and credit amounts exactly in integer cents, and publish balances.csv with invoice_id and outstanding_cents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired utility ran successfully and produced exact balances I100=0, I101=1000, and I102=150. The visible implementation uses integer long values, aggregates payments by invoice, subtracts signed payments from invoice totals, and produced identical output on a repeat run and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2b288753cf014b2a","cmd-99f7740dd9384d0d","cmd-0511ca5b773b42fa","cmd-4f9bf7273ad040fe"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Write unknown invoice IDs and malformed amounts to rejected.csv with a reason.","status":"satisfied","summary":"rejected.csv contains the unknown-invoice payment P4 with reason unknown_invoice_id and malformed payment P5 with reason malformed_amount; an exact-file comparison passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-99f7740dd9384d0d","cmd-0511ca5b773b42fa","cmd-4f9bf7273ad040fe"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Avoid counting a duplicate payment_id twice.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The implementation tracks previously seen payment IDs and ignores later occurrences. The fixture's duplicated -10 credit P3 affected I101 only once, yielding 1000, and the explicit duplicate-credit check passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2b288753cf014b2a","cmd-0511ca5b773b42fa"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve invoices.csv and payments.csv.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both source-file SHA-256 hashes remained identical to the preparation baseline before execution, after reconciliation, and after the node restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-5f63fa19597f4801","cmd-99f7740dd9384d0d","cmd-4f9bf7273ad040fe"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The utility compiled and ran with the installed Python 2.4.3. CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 were unchanged, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5f63fa19597f4801","cmd-2b288753cf014b2a","cmd-4f9bf7273ad040fe","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"All substantive mutations were causally related to installing the repair, publishing and verifying outputs, or performing the mandatory restart protocol. Temporary implementation and expected-output files were removed. The one unnecessary retained mutation was /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log, created by the reboot command and still present after execution; it is bounded and low risk but was not cleaned up. The failed in-place write and post-restart compilation attempt show no evidence of changing state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a2af707a94d04106","cmd-2b288753cf014b2a","cmd-0511ca5b773b42fa","cmd-e6ec78c7200647e6","cmd-20702f38e0ee4f6d","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The repaired Python 2.4-compatible utility generates the required balances and rejection records, deduplicates payment IDs, preserves both inputs, and retains the original OS and kernel. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, the node became unavailable during reboot, a different boot identity appeared, and the utility, data, outputs, release, and kernel were verified after recovery.","limitations":["Functional behavior was exercised against the seeded dataset rather than a separate expanded edge-case fixture; general behavior is additionally supported by direct inspection of the captured implementation.","The lifecycle collector could not inspect failed services through systemd on this legacy host, and its yum package-health probe was unsupported/inconclusive both before and after execution. No executor-caused regression is indicated.","The lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the task directory, so final artifact state relies on the executor's direct post-restart checks and hashes."]}
